title: Keep chain-selection notified when a coalesced approval is only partly valid

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      Defensive hardening of `import_approval` in approval-voting. It handles
      every candidate named in a coalesced `ImportApproval` in one loop,
      writing overlay state and collecting actions as it goes. A per-candidate
      failure in the loop (typically `NoAssignment`) used to return early with
      an empty action list. If an earlier candidate had already completed the
      block, that dropped `Action::NoteApprovedInChainSelection` while the
      overlay still recorded the block as approved.

      This is not reachable from the network: approval-distribution rejects a
      coalesced vote if any candidate in it has no known assignment. GRANDPA
      uses `ApprovedAncestor` and does not depend on
      `ChainSelectionMessage::Approved`.

      A per-candidate failure now skips that candidate and moves on, so the
      valid candidates are imported whatever their order in the vote, and the
      collected actions are always returned. The result is still `Bad` if any
      named candidate failed.

crates:
  - name: polkadot-node-core-approval-voting
    bump: patch
